7
00:00:14,143 --> 00:00:15,982
A chemical from Japan,

8
00:00:15,982 --> 00:00:17,356
a gas from Ukraine,

9
00:00:17,356 --> 00:00:19,353
a metal from China.

10
00:00:19,383 --> 00:00:20,008
Each time,

11
00:00:20,008 --> 00:00:22,378
the chip industry discovered that its

12
00:00:22,378 --> 00:00:24,317
weakest link was not a machine worth

13
00:00:24,317 --> 00:00:26,235
hundreds of millions of dollars,

14
00:00:26,235 --> 00:00:28,667
but something that fits in a truck.

15
00:00:29,117 --> 00:00:36,033
If you like finding the hidden money behind the headlines, hit subscribe and like. It really helps the channel.

16
00:00:47,284 --> 00:00:49,882
What is the most important chemical in

17
00:00:49,882 --> 00:00:51,664
a chip factory?

18
00:00:56,284 --> 00:01:00,094
A strong candidate is photoresist.

19
00:01:00,244 --> 00:01:02,377
It is a light-sensitive liquid spread

20
00:01:02,377 --> 00:01:04,684
across the silicon wafer.

21
00:01:04,854 --> 00:01:07,295
When the lithography machine shines its

22
00:01:07,295 --> 00:01:08,382
pattern of light,

23
00:01:08,382 --> 00:01:10,822
the resist changes wherever the light hits

24
00:01:10,822 --> 00:01:11,644
it.

25
00:01:11,784 --> 00:01:12,381
Wash it,

26
00:01:12,381 --> 00:01:14,440
and the circuit design is left behind

27
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:15,449
on the wafer,

28
00:01:15,449 --> 00:01:17,284
ready to be etched.

29
00:01:17,414 --> 00:01:17,872
No resist,

30
00:01:17,872 --> 00:01:18,624
no pattern.

31
00:01:18,624 --> 00:01:19,933
No pattern,

32
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:21,204
no chip.

33
00:01:21,450 --> 00:01:24,310
And resist is not a commodity.

34
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:27,524
Every new generation of chips needs a

35
00:01:27,524 --> 00:01:28,511
new recipe,

36
00:01:28,511 --> 00:01:30,003
tuned to the light,

37
00:01:30,003 --> 00:01:32,531
the machine and the chemistry of one

38
00:01:32,531 --> 00:01:33,890
factory.

39
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,680
That takes hundreds of test cycles between

40
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:39,570
the resist maker and the chipmaker.

41
00:01:39,830 --> 00:01:41,824
One of the biggest suppliers says

42
00:01:41,824 --> 00:01:44,567
developing a new resist can take up

43
00:01:44,567 --> 00:01:45,915
to two years.

44
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:48,180
For the most advanced chips,

45
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:50,724
made with extreme ultraviolet light,

46
00:01:50,724 --> 00:01:53,380
the market belongs to Japan.

47
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:56,605
According to the research firm QYResearch,

48
00:01:56,605 --> 00:01:58,500
three Japanese companies,

49
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,156
Tokyo Ohka Kogyo,

50
00:02:00,156 --> 00:02:02,291
JSR and Shin-Etsu Chemical,

51
00:02:02,291 --> 00:02:04,930
hold about ninety percent of the world

52
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:06,530
market for EUV resist.

53
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:08,530
It is an estimate.

54
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,506
But it means the most advanced factories

55
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:12,536
in Taiwan,

56
00:02:12,536 --> 00:02:15,707
Korea and America all depend on a

57
00:02:15,707 --> 00:02:18,420
few chemical plants in Japan.

58
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:20,492
And this resist sells for about one

59
00:02:20,492 --> 00:02:23,349
thousand eight hundred dollars a gallon.

60
00:02:23,584 --> 00:02:25,734
And the dependence grows with every

61
00:02:25,734 --> 00:02:27,194
generation.

62
00:02:27,254 --> 00:02:29,778
Moving from three nanometer chips to two

63
00:02:29,778 --> 00:02:32,072
nanometer chips adds more than thirty

64
00:02:32,072 --> 00:02:34,137
percent more layers printed with extreme

65
00:02:34,137 --> 00:02:35,491
ultraviolet light,

66
00:02:35,491 --> 00:02:38,844
according to Korean industry figures.

67
00:02:38,884 --> 00:02:40,465
Each layer needs its own coat of

68
00:02:40,465 --> 00:02:41,120
resist,

69
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,226
and its own mask,

70
00:02:42,226 --> 00:02:44,710
printed on blank plates from yet another

71
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:46,268
Japanese specialist,

72
00:02:46,268 --> 00:02:47,094
Hoya.

73
00:02:47,304 --> 00:02:48,677
The smaller the chip,

74
00:02:48,677 --> 00:02:51,372
the more of these materials it eats.

75
00:02:51,617 --> 00:02:54,017
Let me draw why a tiny market

76
00:02:54,017 --> 00:02:56,217
can hold so much power.

77
00:02:56,417 --> 00:02:58,290
The machine that prints the chip is

78
00:02:58,290 --> 00:03:00,997
worth hundreds of millions of dollars.

79
00:03:01,077 --> 00:03:02,971
The resist on a wafer costs very

80
00:03:02,971 --> 00:03:04,897
little by comparison.

81
00:03:05,077 --> 00:03:07,377
But the factory needs both.

82
00:03:07,417 --> 00:03:09,352
If either one is missing,

83
00:03:09,352 --> 00:03:11,177
the whole line stops.

84
00:03:11,237 --> 00:03:13,907
So the cheapest ingredient can carry the

85
00:03:13,907 --> 00:03:17,177
same power as the most expensive machine.

86
00:03:17,417 --> 00:03:19,492
In twenty nineteen,

87
00:03:19,492 --> 00:03:23,400
one country tested exactly that idea.

88
00:03:29,050 --> 00:03:32,122
What happens when a supplier closes the

89
00:03:32,122 --> 00:03:33,029
tap?

90
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:39,188
On July first,

91
00:03:39,188 --> 00:03:40,557
twenty nineteen,

92
00:03:40,557 --> 00:03:43,343
in a decades-old dispute with South Korea

93
00:03:43,343 --> 00:03:45,409
over wartime forced labour,

94
00:03:45,409 --> 00:03:47,963
Japan announced it would restrict exports

95
00:03:47,963 --> 00:03:50,420
